00:09:05.890 --> 00:09:07.450
Is your house holiday ready?

00:09:07.450 --> 00:09:08.283
Are you and your wife,

00:09:08.283 --> 00:09:09.780
are y'all really into
decorating or anything?

00:09:09.780 --> 00:09:11.170
- Oh yes, oh yes.

00:09:11.170 --> 00:09:15.900
Now this year is
especially exciting because

00:09:15.900 --> 00:09:17.040
every year Catherine and I,

00:09:17.040 --> 00:09:18.780
we argue over,

00:09:18.780 --> 00:09:20.860
first of all, what kind
of lights go on the tree.

00:09:20.860 --> 00:09:23.640
She likes those little, little simple,

00:09:23.640 --> 00:09:24.960
simple, they are beautiful.

00:09:24.960 --> 00:09:26.629
They are beautiful for God's
sakes, wherever she is.

00:09:26.629 --> 00:09:28.490
(laughs)

00:09:28.490 --> 00:09:30.210
But I like those big bulb,

00:09:30.210 --> 00:09:32.740
the colored ones, the
green, blue, orange, red,

00:09:32.740 --> 00:09:34.270
you know those guys.

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.890
And so this year it's my
turn for the big lights.

00:09:37.890 --> 00:09:41.180
But as well, my wife
does not care for tinsel.

00:09:41.180 --> 00:09:44.300
And when I was a kid,
we always had tinsel.

00:09:44.300 --> 00:09:45.850
It was probably lead when I was a kid.

00:09:45.850 --> 00:09:47.370
It was probably not good tinsel to have,

00:09:47.370 --> 00:09:48.700
but I loved that tinsel.

00:09:48.700 --> 00:09:51.000
So this year I get the
big lights and the tinsel.

00:09:51.000 --> 00:09:52.300
So we are ready to go.
- Oh my gosh.

00:09:52.300 --> 00:09:53.133
Here is my thing.

00:09:53.133 --> 00:09:54.350
I'm with your wife, if
she doesn't like tinsel.

00:09:54.350 --> 00:09:56.689
Tinsel is messy.

00:09:56.689 --> 00:09:58.066
- (chuckles) That's exactly why.

00:09:58.066 --> 00:09:59.190
(laughter)
- Okay, yeah.

00:09:59.190 --> 00:10:00.023
Yeah.

00:10:00.023 --> 00:10:01.960
Probably 'cause your wife
is the one picking it up.

00:10:01.960 --> 00:10:03.716
I'm just saying, like, (laughs)

00:10:03.716 --> 00:10:04.549
- That's exactly right.

00:10:04.549 --> 00:10:06.050
- (laughs) Like, that is,

00:10:06.050 --> 00:10:09.370
that will make a good day
go bad real quick, Kyle.

00:10:09.370 --> 00:10:10.203
(laughs)

00:10:10.203 --> 00:10:11.036
No, but that's okay.

00:10:11.036 --> 00:10:12.730
It's your year, you do you.

00:10:12.730 --> 00:10:15.943
So what's the most memorable
Christmas gift you ever got?

00:10:17.773 --> 00:10:20.560
- Oh, I have had a lot
of great Christmases.

00:10:20.560 --> 00:10:22.233
I got a BB gun one year.

00:10:22.233 --> 00:10:23.740
And you know, that's a passage of right.

00:10:23.740 --> 00:10:25.370
A young man gets his first,

00:10:25.370 --> 00:10:26.660
his first rifle.

00:10:26.660 --> 00:10:27.493
- [Kelly] Yeah. (laughs)

00:10:27.493 --> 00:10:30.540
- And my parents went on a vacation.

00:10:30.540 --> 00:10:31.640
They went on a trip somewhere.

00:10:31.640 --> 00:10:33.890
It was my sister who is seven
years old and I at the house.

00:10:33.890 --> 00:10:36.777
And he made it very explicit,

00:10:36.777 --> 00:10:39.720
"Do not touch that BB gun."

00:10:39.720 --> 00:10:40.860
But of course I knew where he hid it.

00:10:40.860 --> 00:10:43.260
He put everything up on
the top of his closet.

00:10:43.260 --> 00:10:44.690
You know, Christmas presents.

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:45.523
They didn't notice it,

00:10:45.523 --> 00:10:47.840
but all of them had little
tears in all the corners,

00:10:47.840 --> 00:10:49.540
'cause I'd been up there like a squirrel

00:10:49.540 --> 00:10:50.919
trying to figure it out.

00:10:50.919 --> 00:10:51.752
(gasps)

00:10:51.752 --> 00:10:52.600
But I took that BB gun out of there

00:10:52.600 --> 00:10:54.970
and my sister said, "What are you doing?"

00:10:54.970 --> 00:10:56.177
I said, "I'm gonna take this outside,

00:10:56.177 --> 00:10:57.530
"and I'm gonna shoot it."

00:10:57.530 --> 00:10:59.770
And she goes, "Well, don't aim that."

00:10:59.770 --> 00:11:02.070
I said, "It's not loaded Kelsey."

00:11:02.070 --> 00:11:03.570
And she goes, "Well, just be careful."

00:11:03.570 --> 00:11:05.320
I said, "It's not loaded,
don't worry about it."

00:11:05.320 --> 00:11:07.460
Now we had this very
beautiful picture window,

00:11:07.460 --> 00:11:09.253
a double pane picture window in Illinois.

00:11:09.253 --> 00:11:10.086
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:11:10.086 --> 00:11:11.300
- And I said, "It's not loaded."

00:11:11.300 --> 00:11:13.450
And so I aimed it and
I pulled the trigger.

00:11:14.310 --> 00:11:15.240
Well, I'll tell you what.

00:11:15.240 --> 00:11:17.590
Right in the middle of
that giant picture window

00:11:17.590 --> 00:11:19.950
was a beautiful little bullet hole.

00:11:19.950 --> 00:11:22.170
You know, just perfect.

00:11:22.170 --> 00:11:23.920
I started crying.

00:11:23.920 --> 00:11:25.700
I cried and cried.

00:11:25.700 --> 00:11:28.450
It was the most terrifying
thing in my life.

00:11:28.450 --> 00:11:31.127
But so, just like Ralphie.

00:11:31.127 --> 00:11:32.620
(laughter)
- Yeah, just like Ralphie.

00:11:32.620 --> 00:11:33.660
I know, I know.

00:11:33.660 --> 00:11:35.772
Don't go sticking your tongue on a pole.

00:11:35.772 --> 00:11:39.761
(upbeat holiday music)

00:11:39.761 --> 00:11:40.594
(audience applauds)
All right.

00:11:40.594 --> 00:11:42.500
So what's your favorite
thing about New York

00:11:42.500 --> 00:11:43.453
at Christmas time?

00:11:44.387 --> 00:11:45.730
- It really is the vibe.

00:11:45.730 --> 00:11:47.220
And it's just a magical place.

00:11:47.220 --> 00:11:49.620
I mean, New York city just has that,

00:11:49.620 --> 00:11:51.240
you know, they just go big.

00:11:51.240 --> 00:11:52.140
I mean, it's like,

00:11:53.890 --> 00:11:56.690
I think the window
shopping is pretty awesome.

00:11:56.690 --> 00:11:59.670
It doesn't get old for
me, whether it be Macy's,

00:11:59.670 --> 00:12:03.500
or you know, FAO, or Saks Fifth Avenue.

00:12:03.500 --> 00:12:05.720
Just going by the windows,
it's all done up beautifully.

00:12:05.720 --> 00:12:06.640
And it's a scene,

00:12:06.640 --> 00:12:09.440
and they spent hours and probably years

00:12:09.440 --> 00:12:11.130
working on those window displays.

00:12:11.130 --> 00:12:13.730
They are just gorgeous for
everybody and it's free.

00:12:13.730 --> 00:12:14.781
- Yeah, and they make you,

00:12:14.781 --> 00:12:15.840
yeah, they make you feel so happy.

00:12:15.840 --> 00:12:16.673
I'm with you.

00:12:16.673 --> 00:12:18.820
And what was like your best
gift that you still remember?

00:12:18.820 --> 00:12:20.180
- Oh, best gift definitely,

00:12:20.180 --> 00:12:21.590
I got an electric guitar.

00:12:21.590 --> 00:12:22.470
I'll never forget it.

00:12:22.470 --> 00:12:25.390
I was probably 12, 13, and I got,

00:12:25.390 --> 00:12:26.610
it was just awesome looking.

00:12:26.610 --> 00:12:29.160
It was a fake Fender Strat.

00:12:29.160 --> 00:12:30.660
It was red and white.

00:12:30.660 --> 00:12:32.900
The name of the company was Phantom.

00:12:32.900 --> 00:12:35.290
But it was so cool and was so,

00:12:35.290 --> 00:12:36.420
I remember being so heavy.

00:12:36.420 --> 00:12:38.520
I was like, I didn't know
guitars were that heavy.

00:12:38.520 --> 00:12:39.460
And I wasn't even that good,

00:12:39.460 --> 00:12:41.430
but I felt like a rock star holding it.

00:12:41.430 --> 00:12:42.640
It was so awesome.

00:12:42.640 --> 00:12:43.473
I love it.

00:12:43.473 --> 00:12:44.410
I love you Santa.

00:12:44.410 --> 00:12:46.480
(laughter)
And I also,

00:12:46.480 --> 00:12:48.140
my worst gift ever was,

00:12:48.140 --> 00:12:48.973
one year,

00:12:48.973 --> 00:12:49.806
I don't know why,

00:12:49.806 --> 00:12:54.790
my Santa Claus got me a DVD
of the movie, "Big Chill."

00:12:55.887 --> 00:12:56.720
- "Big Chill"?

00:12:56.720 --> 00:12:58.460
- Again, I'm like 13 years old.

00:12:58.460 --> 00:13:02.077
So this is a movie about, you
know, midlife crisis. (laughs)

00:13:02.077 --> 00:13:02.910
(laughter)

00:13:02.910 --> 00:13:04.600
I don't know why I'm on the list,

00:13:04.600 --> 00:13:05.945
but I remember going, "Okay."

00:13:05.945 --> 00:13:07.277
(laughter)

00:13:07.277 --> 00:13:08.110
"Big Chill."

00:13:08.110 --> 00:13:10.950
About people trying to have a
baby and stuff like (chuckles)

00:13:10.950 --> 00:13:12.160
yeah, okay.

00:13:12.160 --> 00:13:14.850
But I guess Santa thought the
soundtrack was good (chuckles)

00:13:14.850 --> 00:13:15.683
that I would like it.

00:13:15.683 --> 00:13:16.670
I love it now.

00:13:16.670 --> 00:13:18.920
Now that I'm in my forties. (chuckles)

00:13:18.920 --> 00:13:20.460
But when you are a kid--
- Oh my God.

00:13:20.460 --> 00:13:21.439
That's amazing.

00:13:21.439 --> 00:13:23.750
- No, that was not one of my best gifts.

00:13:23.750 --> 00:13:24.583
- That's a weird gift

00:13:24.583 --> 00:13:26.040
that they definitely
weren't thinking of you

00:13:26.040 --> 00:13:27.227
when they got it. (laughs)

00:13:27.227 --> 00:13:28.168
(laughter)

00:13:28.168 --> 00:13:29.193
They were like, "We forgot."

00:13:29.193 --> 00:13:30.026
- I think Santa was thinking of Santa.

00:13:30.026 --> 00:13:32.840
- "We forgot to get, so we just
pulled something." (laughs)

00:13:32.840 --> 00:13:36.090
(upbeat holiday music)

00:13:38.380 --> 00:13:40.500
Give it up for the lovely
Miss Carrie Underwood.

00:13:40.500 --> 00:13:42.509
(audience applauds)

00:13:42.509 --> 00:13:43.893
(upbeat rock music)

00:13:43.893 --> 00:13:44.813
- Hi.

00:13:44.813 --> 00:13:47.376
- (laughs) Hi.

00:13:47.376 --> 00:13:48.270
How are you?

00:13:48.270 --> 00:13:49.270
- How are you?

00:13:49.270 --> 00:13:50.110
- I am so good.

00:13:50.110 --> 00:13:51.210
I love your red.

00:13:51.210 --> 00:13:52.320
I love it, is it satin?

00:13:52.320 --> 00:13:53.153
That's nice.

00:13:53.153 --> 00:13:53.986
And velvet?

00:13:53.986 --> 00:13:54.845
Or what is that?

00:13:54.845 --> 00:13:55.678
- Yeah.

00:13:55.678 --> 00:13:56.511
- [Kelly[ That's nice.

00:13:56.511 --> 00:13:58.128
- It's like a smoking jacket, I guess.

00:13:58.128 --> 00:13:58.961
That's what you call that?

00:13:58.961 --> 00:13:59.794
- [Kelly] I like it.

00:13:59.794 --> 00:14:01.152
It's very distinguished.

00:14:01.152 --> 00:14:02.010
I like it.
- Yes.

00:14:02.010 --> 00:14:03.890
- It is such a great time

00:14:03.890 --> 00:14:05.760
for you to be releasing this record.

00:14:05.760 --> 00:14:07.570
Everybody needs this kind of hope.

00:14:07.570 --> 00:14:09.740
Everybody needs this, just cheerfulness.

00:14:09.740 --> 00:14:12.000
This reminder that humanity

00:14:12.000 --> 00:14:14.984
is not going down in flames. (laughs)

00:14:14.984 --> 00:14:15.817
(laughter)

00:14:15.817 --> 00:14:17.460
And everything isn't going so poorly.

00:14:17.460 --> 00:14:18.570
Did you feel like inspired

00:14:18.570 --> 00:14:20.410
to do the Christmas record
right now because of that?

00:14:20.410 --> 00:14:21.243
- No.

00:14:21.243 --> 00:14:23.910
I mean, that was kind of after the fact.

00:14:23.910 --> 00:14:26.390
Like, we had started working
on this Christmas album,

00:14:26.390 --> 00:14:28.320
and it was something
I've always wanted to do.

00:14:28.320 --> 00:14:30.370
I knew it was inevitable.

00:14:30.370 --> 00:14:32.370
If you have, you know,

00:14:32.370 --> 00:14:34.310
a career that lasts any timespan at all,

00:14:34.310 --> 00:14:36.130
you are gonna make a Christmas album.

00:14:36.130 --> 00:14:37.320
You just have to.

00:14:37.320 --> 00:14:38.870
And I've always wanted to.

00:14:38.870 --> 00:14:41.320
So we kind of got the wheels in motion

00:14:41.320 --> 00:14:42.730
at the end of last year.

00:14:42.730 --> 00:14:47.110
And then 2020 just dumped
itself in our laps. (laughs)

00:14:47.110 --> 00:14:49.510
And it was just trying to figure out

00:14:49.510 --> 00:14:52.130
how to keep moving
forward and make it happen

00:14:52.130 --> 00:14:54.180
despite 2020.

00:14:54.180 --> 00:14:55.317
- Yeah, definitely, definitely.

00:14:55.317 --> 00:14:57.220
It was a perfect time to release that.

00:14:57.220 --> 00:14:58.750
I'm really happy you are doing it.

00:14:58.750 --> 00:14:59.690
And we just saw,

00:14:59.690 --> 00:15:00.880
I don't know if you've noticed, we saw,

00:15:00.880 --> 00:15:01.713
'cause you are remote,

00:15:01.713 --> 00:15:04.470
but we saw real life
Griswold family house.

00:15:04.470 --> 00:15:07.170
Were you a fan of "National
Lampoon's Christmas Vacation"?

00:15:07.170 --> 00:15:08.580
Or was there another Christmas movie

00:15:08.580 --> 00:15:09.413
that always did it for you,

00:15:09.413 --> 00:15:11.230
that you have to watch every year?

00:15:11.230 --> 00:15:14.850
- I mean, I think everybody is
a fan of "Christmas Vacation"

00:15:14.850 --> 00:15:15.683
right?

00:15:15.683 --> 00:15:16.516
- It's so great.

00:15:16.516 --> 00:15:17.349
- It's a classic.

00:15:17.349 --> 00:15:19.810
I also consider "Die
Hard" a Christmas movie.

00:15:19.810 --> 00:15:20.643
- Oh my gosh!

00:15:20.643 --> 00:15:22.410
I love that "Die Hard."

00:15:22.410 --> 00:15:23.560
First of all, I love all the Die Hards.

00:15:23.560 --> 00:15:25.750
But I love that it's at
Christmas time, the party.

00:15:25.750 --> 00:15:26.583
It counts.
- It is.

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:27.960
It's a Christmas movie.

00:15:27.960 --> 00:15:29.130
- That is a Christmas classic.

00:15:29.130 --> 00:15:29.963
I will go with that.

00:15:29.963 --> 00:15:32.350
Well, I have to ask you about this photo.

00:15:32.350 --> 00:15:34.390
So here, I'm gonna put it up for you.

00:15:34.390 --> 00:15:35.508
This is awesome. (laughs)

00:15:35.508 --> 00:15:36.360
(laughter)

00:15:36.360 --> 00:15:39.070
So, here is the thing I
love about this picture.

00:15:39.070 --> 00:15:42.300
My kids naturally, they
gravitate towards Ursula,

00:15:42.300 --> 00:15:43.140
not Little Mermaid.

00:15:43.140 --> 00:15:45.930
They gravitate towards
Gaston, not The Beast.

00:15:45.930 --> 00:15:47.610
I don't know what's wrong with them.

00:15:47.610 --> 00:15:49.900
But does yours gravitate
towards the Grinch

00:15:49.900 --> 00:15:51.110
(chuckles) instead of Santa?

00:15:51.110 --> 00:15:56.110
- He just loves kind of the
creepy, like aspect of things.

00:15:56.413 --> 00:15:57.960
So he would like,

00:15:57.960 --> 00:15:59.370
like "Nightmare before Christmas"

00:15:59.370 --> 00:16:01.653
which is, you know, a Christmas movie.

00:16:02.520 --> 00:16:04.793
But he likes like the creepyness of it.

00:16:04.793 --> 00:16:06.080
I mean, he loves Santa.

00:16:06.080 --> 00:16:07.423
He has the sweetest heart.

00:16:09.150 --> 00:16:10.110
I don't know.

00:16:10.110 --> 00:16:12.160
He is my child.

00:16:12.160 --> 00:16:14.900
I like scary movies and
the creepy stuff too.

00:16:14.900 --> 00:16:19.900
I swear I have not imposed
any of my stuff onto him.

00:16:20.380 --> 00:16:22.160
This is just what he likes going for us.

00:16:22.160 --> 00:16:23.490
So he loves The Grinch.

00:16:23.490 --> 00:16:24.323
- It's so funny.

00:16:24.323 --> 00:16:25.410
'Cause I'm opposite.

00:16:25.410 --> 00:16:27.670
Like, I don't like anything scary,

00:16:27.670 --> 00:16:29.810
and my kids love it.

00:16:29.810 --> 00:16:31.527
Like, I'm the one sitting
on the couch going,

00:16:31.527 --> 00:16:34.637
"Why can't we just like, watch
like something really happy?

00:16:34.637 --> 00:16:37.040
"Like, (chuckles) why does
everything have to scare me?"

00:16:37.040 --> 00:16:37.873
Speaking of children though,

00:16:37.873 --> 00:16:38.706
Isaiah,

00:16:38.706 --> 00:16:40.210
so, you sang a duet
with him on the record.

00:16:40.210 --> 00:16:42.310
And I saw on the special as well,

00:16:42.310 --> 00:16:43.580
there is video footage of him as well.

00:16:43.580 --> 00:16:46.530
So, was he excited to hear
himself on the record?

00:16:46.530 --> 00:16:47.830
- He was.

00:16:47.830 --> 00:16:49.680
I had no idea what was gonna happen.

00:16:49.680 --> 00:16:52.430
You know, he's never been in
that kind of situation before.

00:16:52.430 --> 00:16:55.000
I don't think he's even been
like in the studio with me

00:16:55.000 --> 00:16:55.930
ever before.

00:16:55.930 --> 00:16:57.230
- [Kelly] Oh.

00:16:57.230 --> 00:17:00.250
- I don't know if he
knows what I do at all,

00:17:00.250 --> 00:17:01.310
but I just thought,

00:17:01.310 --> 00:17:03.690
I could hear his voice on it in my head

00:17:03.690 --> 00:17:05.420
when I was singing it in the studio.

00:17:05.420 --> 00:17:08.270
And I just thought I'd ask him
and see if he might want to.

00:17:08.270 --> 00:17:10.390
And he did such a great job.

00:17:10.390 --> 00:17:11.450
And listening back,

00:17:11.450 --> 00:17:14.140
like, I feel like he is
just so proud of himself.

00:17:14.140 --> 00:17:15.230
And he went to school,

00:17:15.230 --> 00:17:18.107
and he is like, "Hey, my song's out.

00:17:18.107 --> 00:17:19.072
"You wanna hear my song?"

00:17:19.072 --> 00:17:19.905
- [Kelly] My song's out. (laughs)

00:17:19.905 --> 00:17:21.830
- [Carrie] And they were like
listening to it in his class.

00:17:21.830 --> 00:17:23.210
- I think it's adorable.

00:17:23.210 --> 00:17:25.250
And it's cool I think
that, when we are singers,

00:17:25.250 --> 00:17:27.130
that our kids take some kind
of interest in what we do.

00:17:27.130 --> 00:17:28.120
That's kind of cool.

00:17:28.120 --> 00:17:31.370
(upbeat holiday music)

